            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LivelyCow1858"
            },
            "reviewBody": "If you like eggnog, you will love this winter warmer. I like my coffee pretty strong, so next time I think I'll add in an extra shot of espresso. A grating of fresh nutmeg on the top is also a must!",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-02T17:27:39.457Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Holiday Baker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought this tasted pretty good, but you have to really like eggnog to appreciate it. The eggnog taste really comes through. I used a strong brewed coffee and then mixed the eggnog and milk, microwaved them, and then used my Aerolatte whisk. I was told about Silk brand eggnog the other day and used that. For those who can't have eggnog, because of the cholesterol, it is a nice subtitute. The coffee needs a little something else though. I seen on-line that eggnog syrup can be purchased. I am waiting for a recipe for it. Either way, I did top it with a little lite whipped cream and then the nutmeg as suggested. TY",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-13T15:55:51.410Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
